{
  "name": "dung-beetle",
  "_about": "The sacred scarab (Scarabaeus sacer), 3 cm long: broad, flat and matt black; the head a semicircular shield with a rake of six teeth across its front, a short three-leaved antennal club; a wide rounded pronotum; short wing cases with faint grooves; broad front tibiae with four big teeth for digging and no front feet, long middle and hind legs; behind it its BALL of dung, 5 cm across -- twice its own length -- its hind legs up on it pushing, head down (param ball). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
